WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.859
Job one: get the work done.

2
00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:11.374
Why it matters: when people are not sure what is expected, work comes in late, gets redone, or quietly drops,

3
00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:15.671
and you find out on the due date. Four habits fix that.

4
00:00:15.721 --> 00:00:22.076
Plan it: before the quarter starts, pick three priorities, give each one an owner,

5
00:00:22.126 --> 00:00:25.592
and decide what moves if a new request lands.

6
00:00:25.642 --> 00:00:33.325
Say it: every person can tell you, without notes, what they own, by when, and what good looks like,

7
00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:38.247
and it is written where they can see it, not kept in your head.

8
00:00:38.297 --> 00:00:44.340
Check it: look at the work while it is in progress, in your weekly one-on-one,

9
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.543
not the finished product on the due date.

10
00:00:47.593 --> 00:00:53.245
Fix it: when something breaks twice, find the cause and change something,

11
00:00:53.295 --> 00:00:56.604
instead of fixing it a third time yourself.

12
00:00:56.654 --> 00:01:04.885
What to stop doing: assuming the team knows, sending the goal in one email, checking only when it is late,

13
00:01:04.935 --> 00:01:08.713
and doing the work yourself because it is faster.

14
00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:14.650
This week: pick one person and confirm, out loud, what they own and by when.

15
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:22.618
Now flip the four cards on the page; the back of each shows what to stop doing and what to do instead.

